.vercel
.env*

# Runtime binaries: pinned private GitHub staging asset bundle.
/public/ahv/**/*.jpeg
/public/ahv/**/*.jpg
/public/ahv/**/*.mp4
/public/ahv/**/*.pdf
/public/ahv/**/*.png
/public/ahv/**/*.ttf
/public/ahv/**/*.webp

# EXCEPTION: the two routes Abilash ruled BUILD on 2026-09-20.
#
# The ignore rules above exist because the design package's 2,053 runtime
# binaries ship from a pinned GitHub release, hash-verified by
# tools/restore-runtime-assets.mjs, which REFUSES any archive member the
# manifest does not name. These 79 images cannot go in that bundle: they belong
# to /karkidaka-chikitsha-or-monsoon-wellness.html and
# /treatment-in-kerala-russian.html, which the package does not contain, and
# adding them means cutting a new release - an owner action, not an agent one.
#
# So they are tracked here instead, deliberately: 2.3 MB, and the alternative is
# two routes whose pictures exist on one laptop. When the package is next cut
# WITH these routes in it, they move into the bundle and this exception goes.
!/public/ahv/assets/img/legacy/karkidaka-chikitsha-or-monsoon-wellness/**
!/public/ahv/assets/img/legacy/treatment-in-kerala-russian/**

# EXCEPTION: long-form advertising route assets (owner rulings, 2026-09-21).
#
# Same reasoning as the block above, same shape. The long-form advertising
# routes are not in the pinned design package either, so their assets cannot go
# into the hash-verified bundle without cutting a new release - an owner action.
# restore-runtime-assets.mjs only extracts members its manifest names and never
# deletes anything else, so a tracked file here is safe from it.
#
# When the package is next cut WITH these routes in it, these move into the
# bundle and this exception goes, exactly like the one above.
!/public/ahv/assets/img/longform/**
